=== SURVEY ===
vehicle_config_repo.go references table vehicle_config_snapshots which does not exist.
Migration 000142 consolidated it into vehicle_meta_snapshots (category='config').
Columns available for config: car_type, exterior_color, wheel_type, software_version, spoiler_type, has_ludicrous_mode.
Callers: telemetry_handler.go:2222 (Insert), vehicle_config_handler.go:27,45 (GetByVehicle, GetLatest).

=== REASONING ===
Option A chosen: rewrite repo to INSERT/SELECT from vehicle_meta_snapshots WHERE category='config'.
- Insert: maps CarType, ExteriorColor, WheelType, Version→software_version. Uses Exec (no RETURNING id since new table has composite PK).
- ON CONFLICT upsert with COALESCE to preserve non-null values on concurrent inserts.
- GetByVehicle: selects mapped columns, orders by ts DESC, maps ts→CreatedAt.
- Fields without columns (trim, roof_color, rear_seat_heaters, etc.) silently dropped on insert, returned as nil on select.
- Model unchanged (pointer types handle nil gracefully).
- telemetry_handler.go unchanged (still builds full model; Insert ignores unmapped fields).

=== CHANGES ===
internal/database/vehicle_config_repo.go:
  - INSERT → vehicle_meta_snapshots with category='config', ON CONFLICT upsert
  - SELECT → vehicle_meta_snapshots WHERE category='config' ORDER BY ts DESC
  - Removed RETURNING id (composite PK, no serial id column)
  - Added time.Now() for ts column on insert
  - Reduced column list to match vehicle_meta_snapshots config columns

